WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.329 --> 00:00:05.660
Jaime Lannister: As the saying goes, "Every
time a Targaryen is born, the gods flip a

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:06.660
coin."

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.719
They must have dropped the one for King Aerys,
for at first, he seemed to have dodged the

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:13.059
family madness.

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:17.670
But as he grew older, he began to see conspirators
everywhere, and where there were none, he

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:18.920
worked to create them.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:24.860
As one of his Kingsguard, I saw firsthand
that a king who couldn't rule his own mind

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.039
couldn't rule Seven Kingdoms.

00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:31.290
We endured his reign because we hoped his
son Rhaegar would ride the rail when he ascended

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.310
to the throne.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:37.650
But then Rhaegar proved as mad as his father
and snatched Lyanna Stark, daughter of the

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:41.610
Warden of the North and betrothed to Robert
Baratheon, Lord of the Stormlands.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:48.750
When Lyanna's father and eldest brother demanded
justice, the Mad King obliged, laughing as

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.680
he dispensed it.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.941
Varys: Unsatisfied with only two murders,
the Mad King then ordered Jon Arryn, Lord

00:00:55.941 --> 00:01:02.010
of the Vale, to execute his two wards, Robert
Baratheon and Eddard Stark.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:06.040
Instead, Jon Arryn raised the Vale in revolt.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:11.600
Ned Stark slipped past royalist sentries and
raised the North, and Robert won three battles

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:18.050
in a single day to unite the Stormlands behind
them, only to be defeated by a royalist army

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:22.180
and forced to flee, leaving his home of Storm's
End besieged.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:27.280
Sansa Stark: The Hand of the King finally
cornered Robert in the town of the Stoney

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.310
Sept and sent his soldiers door-to-door, searching
for the rebel leader.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:36.700
But the villagers hated the Mad King and loved
Robert, and kept him one step ahead of the

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.700
soldiers until only one refuge remained.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.090
As the soldiers closed in, all the town bells
rang out.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:49.140
Hearing of Robert's plight, our father and
Jon Arryn had rushed to the Riverlands and

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:52.750
enlisted our grandfather, Hoster Tully, to
help them.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:57.140
Together, they routed the Hand's army and
rescued Robert.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:02.100
To celebrate and cement the Tully alliance,
our father wed our mother, Catelyn, and Jon

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.420
Arryn took our aunt, Lysa.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:10.479
Only a fortnight later, both men rushed back
into the field, for the dragon had finally

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:11.479
woken.

00:02:11.479 --> 00:02:17.030
Viserys: While my father's servants were losing
my father's kingdoms, my brother Rhaegar had

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:21.190
been cooped up with his...Mistress?

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:24.090
Whatever else, I'd call her a distraction.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.840
But now Rhaegar came to his senses and returned
to King's Landing.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:34.190
He persuaded our father to summon his estranged
friend, Lord Tywin Lannister, the richest

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:36.660
and most powerful lord in the realm.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:42.540
Rhaegar himself would lead the royal army
against the usurper, Robert.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:47.841
On the banks of the Trident, my brother fought
the man whose wife he had stolen, and who

00:02:47.841 --> 00:02:51.200
fought to steal his birthright in return.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.870
In the end, Robert wanted it more.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:02.319
His hammer shattered my brother's armor, and
its rubies fell into the river like raindrops,

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:04.610
vanishing in the current.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:10.890
Varys: With Rhaegar's defeat, nothing stood
between Robert and King's Landing.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:17.200
Imagine the King's surprise a fortnight later
when he saw not stags, but lions outside his

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.380
gates.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:23.760
His former Hand, Tywin Lannister, had come
to the capital with a force even Robert couldn't

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.030
match, claiming to be loyal to the king.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:31.980
Trusting what he wanted to believe, Aerys
ordered the gates opened, and the Lannister

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:39.099
forces dutifully began to pillage, and murder
the king's actual loyal subjects.

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:44.270
When Eddard Stark finally arrived at the capital
with Robert's army, he found Lannister banners

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:51.010
hanging over the sacked city, Targaryen corpses
littering its streets and Ser Jaime Lannister

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:52.860
sitting on the Iron Throne.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:04:00.010
Below him, the Mad King Aerys, whom Ser Jaime
had sworn to guard, lay in a pool of his own

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:04.290
blood from a sword thrust through his back.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.900
Lord Eddard might've thanked Ser Jaime for
doing the realm a favor, but honorable as

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:16.440
he was, Lord Eddard condemned Ser Jaime as
a "Kingslayer," a name he would never escape.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:23.410
Jaime: Unlike Lord Eddard, Robert appreciated
my contribution to his glorious victory.

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:27.939
He pardoned me for my crime and even kept
me on his Kingsguard beside Ser Barristan

00:04:27.939 --> 00:04:31.610
Selmy, who'd been wounded at the Trident fighting
for Rhaegar.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:37.309
True, both of us had failed to protect out
Targaryen charges, but perhaps that's what

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:39.559
Robert liked most about us.

00:04:39.559 --> 00:04:44.699
When my father presented Robert with the bodies
of Rhaegar's wife and two children, Ned Stark

00:04:44.699 --> 00:04:49.879
hiked up his skirt and demanded Robert send
their killer to Dorne and me to the Wall.

00:04:49.879 --> 00:04:53.110
But I saw what Ned couldn't.

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:59.639
Robert was ashamed of the bodies and more
ashamed of his relief.

00:04:59.639 --> 00:05:04.419
He knew that Rhaegar's heirs had to die, or
his throne would never be safe.

00:05:04.419 --> 00:05:07.819
But glorious heroes didn't kill children.

00:05:07.819 --> 00:05:11.400
They simply didn't punish their murderers.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:17.539
Varys: For three hundred years, the Targaryen
dynasty ruled Westeros.

00:05:17.539 --> 00:05:23.509
Wars were still fought, homes still burned
and men still died, but compared to the chaos

00:05:23.509 --> 00:05:26.879
of what came before, the realm was stable.

00:05:26.879 --> 00:05:29.669
Petyr Baelish: And boring.

00:05:29.669 --> 00:05:34.419
The Targaryens lied, thieved and killed as
much as other lords.

00:05:34.419 --> 00:05:38.710
They just had dragons to answer all complaints.

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.969
Until they didn't.

00:05:40.969 --> 00:05:46.430
When the last dragon died, it was only a matter
of time before the Targaryens followed.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:50.009
Varys: By "only," you mean another century?

00:05:50.009 --> 00:05:55.759
Baelish: Which they wasted trying to replace
their lost advantage: incinerating their own

00:05:55.759 --> 00:06:02.059
palaces to hatch dragon eggs, drinking wildfire
to become dragons, and, let's not forget the

00:06:02.059 --> 00:06:07.539
Mad King's favorite, burning men alive so
he could pretend to be a dragon.

00:06:07.539 --> 00:06:11.439
Varys: We urged Aerys to pardon Brandon Stark.

00:06:11.439 --> 00:06:16.339
The boy had threatened Prince Rhaegar, but
Rhaegar had stolen the boy's sister, and the

00:06:16.339 --> 00:06:19.680
boy was the eldest son of our Warden of the
North.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:25.289
Baelish: Who is the greater fool: a mad king
or the man who reasons with him?

00:06:25.289 --> 00:06:28.289
Aerys saw knives in every shadow.

00:06:28.289 --> 00:06:33.780
When you told him to treat the Starks with
caution, you made him afraid and what he feared

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:34.849
he killed.

00:06:34.849 --> 00:06:39.130
Varys: I wouldn't have thought you of all
people would bother with recriminations for

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:41.689
Brandon's death, Lord Baelish.

00:06:41.689 --> 00:06:45.250
Not after your, shall we call it, "duel" with
him?

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:52.319
Baelish: Brandon was as arrogant as he was
stupid; like his father, Lord Stark, who answered

00:06:52.319 --> 00:06:53.659
Aerys' summon to the capital.

00:06:53.659 --> 00:06:56.099
They earned their fates.

00:06:56.099 --> 00:07:00.059
But the younger son, Ned, what was his crime?

00:07:00.059 --> 00:07:02.289
That Aerys ordered his death as well?

00:07:02.289 --> 00:07:06.069
Varys: Unlike men, families do not die when
you lop off their head.

00:07:06.069 --> 00:07:11.559
Baelish: At the very least, you should have
pointed out that loyal and dutiful Ned was

00:07:11.559 --> 00:07:17.270
living with Jon Arryn, a proud and over-righteous
lord with an impregnable castle and no sons

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.159
of his own.

00:07:19.159 --> 00:07:22.560
Perhaps you could have spared Aerys the "embarrassment"
of revolt.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:28.169
Varys: If only we'd had the foresight to consult
you, Lord Baelish, but I suppose first we'd

00:07:28.169 --> 00:07:30.110
have had to know who you were.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:35.620
Baelish: Nobody knew Robert Baratheon either,
yet he claimed the right to sit on the Iron

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:36.620
Throne.

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:39.590
Varys: He had Targaryen blood through his
mother.

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:45.870
Baelish: A pretty dress for an ugly truth:
it was war; and he could swing a hammer harder

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:48.509
than the other options.

00:07:48.509 --> 00:07:50.740
When did you know you'd lost, Lord Varys?

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:54.999
Varys: When Robert Baratheon killed Prince
Rhaegar on the Trident.

00:07:54.999 --> 00:07:56.879
Baelish: Wrong.

00:07:56.879 --> 00:08:01.229
You lost the war when you let Ned Stark slip
back into The North.

00:08:01.229 --> 00:08:05.879
Neither the Bloody Gate of the Vale or Moat
Cailin in the North have ever fallen.

00:08:05.879 --> 00:08:11.300
They could have held out for years even if
you'd killed Robert, but you let him slip

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.160
through your fingers as well.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:17.680
Varys: I told the court that Robert was hiding
in the Stoney Sept, but the Hand of the King

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:21.219
wasted too much time searching the city.

00:08:21.219 --> 00:08:23.860
Something about the glory of single combat.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:28.110
Then Ned Stark's army arrived to save the
day.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.259
Baelish: Too bad Lord Tywin wasn't Hand any
longer.

00:08:31.259 --> 00:08:35.400
He would have simply razed the town and been
done with it.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:36.670
Varys: Perhaps.

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:40.780
And perhaps the rebels would have found even
more of the countryside flocking to their

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:41.780
banners.

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:42.890
Baelish: I'd almost forgotten.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:48.180
You weren't always so loyal to the Lannisters
during the war, were you?

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:51.880
Varys: I did my duty to the realm.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:56.980
When Lord Tywin showed up at King's Landing
professing loyalty, I warned Aerys not to

00:08:56.980 --> 00:08:58.240
open the gates.

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:00.900
Prince Rhaegar was dead, our army scattered.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:04.980
"The lion does not stir unless he smells meat."

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:08.910
Baelish: I admire your powers of persuasion,
Lord Varys.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:12.920
Few could traffic on so many secrets to so
little avail.

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:18.830
Varys: Grand Maester Pycelle told Aerys what
he wanted to hear, that his old friend Tywin

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:20.660
was there to save him.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:26.820
Baelish: Then Aerys's "old friend" sacked
the city, and his son stabbed Aerys in the

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:27.820
back.

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:30.530
Varys: A regrettable though necessary action.

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:36.130
Baelish: As were the pardons the new King
Robert bestowed upon the royalists: Mace Tyrell,

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.360
Barristan Selmy, you.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:42.390
Varys: King Robert wisely chose order over
vengeance.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:46.140
Baelish: Jon Arryn wisely chose for Robert.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:50.510
But Jon Arryn died, then Robert, then Ned.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:53.030
So ended their glorious revolution.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:58.240
Margaery Tyrell: Under the Targaryen dynasty,
Westeros prospered.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:03.190
Gone were the petty wars of Seven Kingdoms
and the endless thirst for minor glories that

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.450
drove them.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:10.900
The Westerlands enriched the realm, the North
guarded it, and the Reach and Riverlands fed

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:12.390
it.

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:18.360
This harmony is what Robert Baratheon shattered
with his rebellion against Aerys Targaryen.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.480
When the call to arms came, though, we did
not want to answer.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:28.720
The Reach is a gentle land, and, honestly,
the Mad King was not much loved.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:32.020
But we owed peace and status to his family.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:38.110
My father, Mace Tyrell, called his banners
and marched north to battle the rogue Storm

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:43.090
Lord, Robert, who had already defeated three
forces in a single day.

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:49.200
And, at Ashford, my father won.

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:53.680
Some chasten my father for not pursuing Robert
after the battle.

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:59.380
We had cut him off from the Stormlands, the
seat of his power, and he had fled north,

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:05.180
within easy grasp of Lord Tywin Lannister,
the Hand of Aerys for twenty years.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:11.150
My father moved instead to lay siege of Robert's
ancestral stronghold of Storm's End.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:15.370
The rose would strangle the stag as the lion
pounced.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.370
So we waited.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:23.480
But the lion slumbered, and Robert slipped
past the King's forces to join Ned Stark.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:28.540
We could have lifted the siege and deployed
our armies north to aid the Crown.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:34.110
We could have stormed the walls of the castle
and made Robert homeless.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:42.920
But we had ample supplies, control of land
and sea, and, most of all, patience.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:50.750
Our siege would succeed, eventually, at little
cost of life to us.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:56.290
If Robert prolonged the war with minor victories,
our capture of Storm's End would hasten his

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.470
downfall.

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:04.310
And if Robert won the war, well, it would
not do for him to find us within his walls

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:07.970
with the bodies of his brother Stannis and
his sworn men.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:15.040
When the lion finally showed his colors and
"purged" King's Landing, we knew our cause

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.160
was lost.

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:22.350
My father chose the peaceful route and bent
the knee to Robert, who heartily pardoned

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:23.810
us.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:29.010
Strange, considering how we had beaten him
and starved his brother to the brink of death.

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:35.350
Catelyn Stark: When I came of age, Brandon
Stark of Winterfell sought and won my hand.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:40.610
To my father, Brandon was heir to the North
and a suitable match for a daughter of House

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.040
Tully.

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:49.130
To me, Brandon was wild and terrifying, never
far from laughter or trouble.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:56.610
I loved him with all the fire of a first passion;
much, I came to realize, as Petyr loved me.

00:12:56.610 --> 00:13:01.680
When Petyr heard of my engagement, he challenged
Brandon to a duel.

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:06.000
Petyr survived only because I begged Brandon
not to kill him.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:09.630
I still thought of Petyr as family.

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:14.670
Now, I wish I had let him die.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:19.510
Only days before my wedding, when I thought
I would be happy forever, Prince Rhaegar Targaryen

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:22.090
abducted Brandon's sister, Lyanna.

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:27.750
Hotblooded as always, Brandon immediately
rode for King's Landing to demand justice,

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:34.810
which the Mad King Aerys Targaryen gave him,
in his own twisted fashion.

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:39.611
The day the raven arrived with news of my
Brandon's death, I locked myself in my room

00:13:39.611 --> 00:13:45.980
and refused to eat for days, until my father
reminded me of my duty.

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:53.320
I was to marry Eddard, Brandon's younger brother,
a man whom I had never met, of whom none spoke

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:58.240
ill or spoke anything at all.

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:04.170
Our union would cement an alliance of the
North, Vale, Stormlands, and Riverlands in

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:07.779
rebellion against the Mad King.

00:14:07.779 --> 00:14:09.650
I was Tully.

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:11.980
I did my duty.

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:17.630
We were married quickly and were spared only
one night before he had to return to the field.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:23.320
I spent the war by the window, waiting for
a raven to hear if my child would grow fatherless,

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:24.960
or at all.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:27.340
We knew the price of defeat.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:32.960
I scoured the kitchens and washing rooms for
any and all gossip.

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:35.920
Robert had won and crushed the Mad King!

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:38.960
Robert had lost, but Jaime Lannister was now
King.

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:44.360
Robert had almost won, but the Mad King had
become a dragon and burned King's Landing

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:45.540
to ash.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:55.220
At night, I told myself the war would end
soon and bring peace: either a victory or

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:57.029
the grave.

00:14:57.029 --> 00:14:59.740
I was wrong.

00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:04.120
Robert won, and my husband avenged his brother
and my love.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:11.320
But when he came home to me, he could not
meet my eyes.

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:15.770
I saw the reason by his side.

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:21.490
Many men have bastards, I know, and under
the strain of war, any man, no matter how

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:26.990
honorable, may forsake his vows for a night
of warmth that he may never know again.

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:30.790
But Ned Stark was not built like other men.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:36.750
His northern honor would not let him sequester
his shame in some distant holdfast.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:42.790
Barristan Selmy: All I ever wanted was to
live a life of honor, defending a king worthy

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.230
of service.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:49.830
During the War of the Ninepenny Kings, I sought
out Maelys the Monstrous, last of the Blackfyre

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:52.850
pretenders, who had started this whole war.

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:57.380
Maelys believed that his Targaryen blood gave
him a claim to the Iron Throne.

00:15:57.380 --> 00:16:03.310
I made sure that his blood claimed nothing
more than the dirt around his corpse.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:07.170
To show his gratitude, the King elevated me
to his Kingsguard.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:11.160
It was the proudest moment of my life.

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:14.960
But that king died, and I wasn't with him.

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:17.430
Not that I could have saved him if I had been.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:22.670
But still, I vowed to do better with his son,
young Prince Aerys.

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:27.520
For twenty years, his reign was peaceful and
prosperous.

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:31.480
Aerys was well-loved by his subjects and respected
by his lords.

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:35.400
But as years went on, Aerys' temper soured.

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:40.550
He became obsessed with dragons and fire,
and the swords of the Kingsguard couldn't

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:45.290
defend him from the enemies he saw lurking
in every shadow.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:49.510
My king went mad.

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:53.560
But there was hope; his son and heir.

00:16:53.560 --> 00:16:58.650
Prince Rhaegar was everything a kingdom could
hope for in a ruler; he was strong but gentle,

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:02.100
wise and cautious, and a good friend.

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:08.029
No matter the wounds Aerys dug into the realm,
we had faith that his son would sew it back

00:17:08.029 --> 00:17:12.250
together again when he ascended the throne.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:17.600
Then came Lord Whent's tourney at Harrenhal,
the largest ever in Westeros.

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:22.679
I unhorsed every man against me until only
Prince Rhaegar remained.

00:17:22.679 --> 00:17:29.950
We each set our feet in our saddles and lowered
our lances and charged, and I fell.

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:34.220
Muddy and bruised, I then watched Rhaegar
present Lyanna Stark with the victor's crown

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:39.860
of roses, though she was betrothed to Robert
Baratheon and Rhaegar himself was married

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:41.629
to Elia Martell.

00:17:41.629 --> 00:17:42.929
We all know what happened after.

00:17:42.929 --> 00:17:48.200
If I had I been a bit quicker with my lance,
had I chosen a faster horse, perhaps I could

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:51.190
have spared the kingdom from the destruction
that came after.

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:56.230
Or if I had thought to warn Brandon Stark
against his rashness.

00:17:56.230 --> 00:18:00.230
He came to King's Landing himself demanding
Rhaegar return his sister.

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:01.250
Poor fool.

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:07.450
If he had only known the depth of Aerys' madness,
he wouldn't have dared provoke him.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:12.009
Aerys ordered Brandon imprisoned, while I
could do nothing but obey.

00:18:12.009 --> 00:18:17.159
When Brandon's father, Lord Rickard Stark,
came to King's Landing to beg for his son,

00:18:17.159 --> 00:18:21.100
Aerys burned him alive, while I could do nothing
but watch.

00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:31.419
I had sworn a vow to a mad king and was honor-bound
to obey him, even at the cost of my soul.

00:18:31.419 --> 00:18:36.639
Ravens soon arrived with dark news for the
king; The Vale was in open revolt.

00:18:36.639 --> 00:18:42.369
Demanding Lyanna Stark's return, Robert Baratheon
was smashing any army that dared face him.

00:18:42.369 --> 00:18:47.570
Eddard Stark, Brandon's younger brother, was
marching the whole of the North down the Neck

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:53.350
and had taken Catelyn Tully, Brandon's betrothed,
for his own, thus winning the support of The

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.559
Riverlands.

00:18:54.559 --> 00:19:00.850
The king sent ravens to Casterly Rock to beg
his former Hand, Tywin Lannister, for help,

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:02.570
and no ravens returned.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:09.059
A plan was devised; Prince Rhaegar would personally
lead the royal forces, now reinforced with

00:19:09.059 --> 00:19:15.049
ten thousand Dornishmen, north to face Robert,
while the Kingsguard, Lewyn Martell and I,

00:19:15.049 --> 00:19:17.059
would ride with the prince.

00:19:17.059 --> 00:19:21.250
Before we left, the prince confided in me
that when he returned from this battle, there

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:23.649
would be a great many changes in court.

00:19:23.649 --> 00:19:27.690
Despite my vows to the king, I confess I was
excited.

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:32.070
On the march to face Robert's army, we were
sure we would win.

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:35.519
We had superior numbers and we had Prince
Rhaegar.

00:19:35.519 --> 00:19:40.299
His presence lifted the spirits of our men
and he looked every inch the king he was destined

00:19:40.299 --> 00:19:41.730
to become.

00:19:41.730 --> 00:19:44.830
But at the Trident the gods played a cruel
joke.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:49.340
Robert proved the Baratheon words as his army
smashed through our lines.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:55.980
Lewyn Martell was killed, I fell in combat
badly wounded and could do nothing but watch

00:19:55.980 --> 00:20:04.039
as Robert's war hammer ended Rhaegar's glorious
reign before it began, and the kingdom that

00:20:04.039 --> 00:20:09.600
would never be washed away down the Trident
with his life's blood.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:16.549
Yet Robert spared me, insisting his personal
Maester tend to my wounds out of respect.

